    intro: "Anyone who has watched birds at dawn, fish in a river or animals at a waterhole has felt the wonder of life's variety. Genesis tells us that God made this variety on purpose. He filled the waters with living things and the sky with birds and then the land with creatures of every kind, and he blessed them.",
    context: "Genesis 1:20-25 completes the filling of the realms that days one to three had formed: the seas and sky on day five, the land on day six. In many ancient stories sea monsters were gods of chaos; Genesis names even the great sea creatures as created beings. Psalm 104 delights in the variety of animals and says they all look to God to give them their food in due season.",
