    apply: "Write a one-page summary of the first twelve lessons with a Scripture reference for each key idea. Review it twice before the test and teach one idea to someone at home. Thank God for each lesson in prayer.",
    activity: "Play a team review game: the teacher reads a clue (for example 'made from dust') and teams call out the topic and a passage. Give extra points for application. End by reading Psalm 8 together.",
    takeHome: "Prepare for the test by reviewing the revision map and memory verses. Write five practice questions of your own, with answers, and test someone.",
    prayer: "Thank God for the first twelve lessons. Ask for clear minds and humble hearts. Praise him as the Creator of all.",
    teacher: "Encourage and review. Go through the revision map and spend more time where learners are unsure. Explain how the test will work: time, number of questions, when results are released. If the test is held in this lesson time, give instructions clearly and allow enough time.",
